course: dictionary
lesson: 11982
title: Cerebral: the brain and the mind
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Cerebral is an adjective with two meanings. The first is about the brain, especially its main part, the cerebrum. «The doctor studied the cerebral scan to see how the brain was working.» The words scan and brain are the clues: a cerebral scan is a picture of the brain.
explain: The second meaning is about thinking. A cerebral person uses the mind more than the feelings. «The cerebral film had no car chases, only long talks about big ideas.» The clues are long talks and big ideas, which show that the film makes you think hard rather than just feel excited.
explain: Cerebral palsy is a health phrase. It is a condition that affects movement and begins from birth. To test your guess, swap in a simpler word such as brain or thinking and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Cerebral» means to do with the brain, especially the cerebrum, which is its main part.
fact: «Cerebral» can also mean thinking a lot in a clever, serious way, using the mind more than the feelings.
fact: «Cerebral palsy» is a condition that affects movement and begins from birth.
fact: A cerebral film or character makes you think hard, rather than just feel excited or scared.
exercise: «The doctor studied the cerebral scan to see how the brain was working.» What does cerebral mean here? | *To do with the brain | To do with the feet | To do with the teeth | To do with the heart
exercise: «The cerebral film had no car chases, only long talks about big ideas.» What kind of film is it? | Full of animals | Funny and silly | *One that makes you think hard | Loud and fast
exercise: «Mia is so cerebral that she would rather solve a puzzle than dance.» What does cerebral suggest about Mia? | She is always singing | She is very sleepy | *She uses her mind more than her feelings | She is afraid of puzzles
test: «Cerebral palsy is a condition that affects movement and begins from birth.» What does this tell us? | *It affects how the body moves, from birth | It only affects the eyes | It is a type of fever | It is caught from other people
test: Jo spent an hour thinking carefully, then gave a cerebral answer. What does cerebral mean here? | *Clever and serious, using the mind | Loud and quick | About the stomach | Made of stone
exam: Which sentence uses cerebral correctly? | «The cerebral cake was very sweet.» | «The cerebral bus was late.» | «The cerebral dog barked at the cat.» | *«The cerebral film made me think for hours.»
